# VENDORED FROM receipt-verifier — DO NOT EDIT IN PLACE.
#
# These are byte-for-byte copies of the shared verification core. A local edit here would be a
# second implementation wearing the first one's name, which is the exact failure 1423 came from:
# conformance had its own idea of what checking meant and it was weaker than prove's.
#
# test/vendor-parity.test.js re-derives these hashes, and compares them against the source repo
# when it is present beside this one. Absent, it says so and checks the pin only — an honest
# skip, never a silent pass.
#
# verify-grant.js is vendored from the WORKING TREE (the two RESERVED INERT v2 fields —
# call_hash, executor_image_digest — are admitted and read by nothing; measured zero behaviour
# change on every shipped capture, positive and negative).
# verify-attest.js is vendored from the WORKING TREE (1465 — the E2E profile now re-verifies
# the executor's attestation from its bytes instead of re-reporting the producer's grade).
# verified-execution-binding.js is vendored from the WORKING TREE (1465 — closed assurance
# profiles). Re-pin to a commit once receipt-verifier commits it; the parity test compares the
# bytes against the sibling checkout, so a working-tree vendor is checked, not merely asserted.
# source_commit: 7887719fa6e2bd1f70907f119e1c2a9b7c6a84ff (evidence-root.js and verify-evidence.js re-vendored for 1432)

